# v0.8 local device-probing artifacts — NEVER commit these.
# They carry real device serials/IPs/credentials-read paths. Test fixtures
# live under tests/fixtures_v08/ and ARE tracked (sanitized); these
# repo-root probe outputs are throwaway.
probe_captures/
probe_captures_v08/
probe_devices.local.json
*.local.json
probe_*.py
probe_*.log
verify_*.py
analyze_*.py
# Sanitizing tooling — sanitize_scan.py hard-codes the REAL camera names
# it looks for, so committing it would re-publish exactly what the
# sanitizing pass just removed. The real->placeholder mapping table itself
# lives outside the repo (../sanitize_map.local.json) and holds real
# serials/MACs; *.local.json below would catch it too.
sanitize_*.py
api_push_*.py
create_release*.py
wait_and_release.py
deprecate_*.py
diagnose_*.py
check_*.py
fix_remote_eol.py
# NOTE on the two lines below: a .gitignore rule has NO effect on a file
# git already tracks. test_new_endpoints.py is tracked (committed in an
# earlier release), so its rule here is a no-op kept only as intent —
# excluding it from a commit needs `git restore --staged`, not this rule.
# test_isapi_endpoints.ps1 is untracked, so its rule does apply.
# Neither script contains a plaintext password: both take it via a
# required --password argument (verified 2026-10-04).
test_isapi_endpoints.ps1
test_new_endpoints.py
# One fixture has a non-ASCII filename (fragile across platform checkouts).
# It is a byte-identical duplicate of a capture already kept under the
# ignored probe_captures_v08/, and no test reads it — so exclude it.
#
# Do NOT use a negated character class here. Git's glob does not support
# \x escapes: `*[^\x00-\x7F]*` is parsed as the literal set [^x0-7F],
# which matches *every* fixture (verified with an untracked probe file)
# and would silently drop all of tests/fixtures_v08 from a fresh clone.
tests/fixtures_v08/*Q_scheme*

# v0.9 one-off tooling — repo-root only (anchored with a leading slash so
# these patterns do NOT reach into tests/, where test_v09_*.py and
# tests/fixtures_v09/ ARE meant to be tracked).
#
# Why these must never be committed: several of them embed the REAL
# identifiers they hunt for. fix_v09_leak.py hard-codes real serial
# tails, scan_residue_v*.py carries the full needle list, and
# prep_filter_repo_rules.py emits the real->placeholder mapping.
# Committing any of them would re-publish exactly what the sanitizing
# pass removed — the same mistake v0.8 made with sanitize_scan.py.
#
# NOTE: a .gitignore rule has NO effect on files git already tracks.
# All of the below are untracked as of v0.9 (verified 2026-10-10),
# so these rules do apply.
/fix_*.py
/scan_*.py
/selftest_*.py
/survey_*.py
/sync_*.py
/gate_*.py
/push_*.py
/prep_*.py
/reaudit_*.py
/recheck_*.py
/adjudicate_*.py
/drill_*.py
/rewrite_*.py
# v0.9 local artifacts: probe outputs, drill clones, scan reports.
/probe_captures_v09/
/_rewrite_drill_*/
/v09_*.txt
/v09_*.json
/v08_verify_final.json
